{"name":"Forestry","hex":"#2f441f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"forestry","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The science of planting and growing trees in forests.","The art and practice of planting and growing trees in forests."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/forestry"}],"entries":[{"title":"Forestry","blocks":[{"text":"Forestry is the science and craft of creating, managing, planting, using, conserving and repairing forests and woodlands for associated resources for human and environmental benefits. Forestry is practiced in plantations and natural stands. The science of forestry has elements that belong to the biological, physical, social, political and managerial sciences. Forest management plays an essential role in creating and modifying habitats, and affects ecosystem services provisioning. A practitioner of forestry is a forester."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/TJ_harvesteri.jpg/330px-TJ_harvesteri.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forestry"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Sylva_paper_1662.jpg/120px-Sylva_paper_1662.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Sylva_paper_1662.jpg/250px-Sylva_paper_1662.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Sylva_paper_1662.jpg/120px-Sylva_paper_1662.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASylva_paper_1662.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Land_Army_girls_sawing_larch_poles_for_use_as_pit_props_at_the_Women%27s_Timber_Corps_training_camp_at_Culford_in_Suffolk._TR912.jpg/250px-Land_Army_girls_saw